    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Compiles to a target-specific software breakpoint instruction or equivalent.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2099,
            2179
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2180,
            2183
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This will typically abort the program. It may result in a core dump, and/or the system logging",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2184,
            2282
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " debug information. Additional target-specific capabilities may be possible depending on",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2283,
            2374
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " debuggers or other tooling; in particular, a debugger may be able to resume execution.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2375,
            2465
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2466,
            2469
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " If possible, this will produce an instruction sequence that allows a debugger to resume *after*",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2470,
            2569
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the breakpoint, rather than resuming *at* the breakpoint; however, the exact behavior is",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2570,
            2662
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " target-specific and debugger-specific, and not guaranteed.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2663,
            2725
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2726,
            2729
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " If the target platform does not have any kind of debug breakpoint instruction, this may compile",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2730,
            2829
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " to a trapping instruction (e.g. an undefined instruction) instead, or to some other form of",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2830,
            2925
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " target-specific abort that may or may not support convenient resumption.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2926,
            3002
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3003,
            3006
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The precise behavior and the precise instruction generated are not guaranteed, except that in",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3007,
            3104
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " normal execution with no debug tooling involved this will not continue executing.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3105,
            3190
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3191,
            3194
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " - On x86 targets, this produces an `int3` instruction.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3195,
            3253
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " - On aarch64 targets, this produces a `brk #0xf000` instruction.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3254,
            3322
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
